'=============================================================================
'
'  Stratus AS3935 Lightning Detection System
'  C2 continuity test, logger used as the meter
'
'  Property of METRON (PTY) LTD [Inteltronics]
'  Developer: L.J. Esterhuizen
'
'=============================================================================
' Site: QUAGGASKLIP
'
' TEMPORARY DIAGNOSTIC. Stores nothing. Load it, run the toggle on the Pi, read
' C2Changes, then put QK_CR300_Lightning.CR300 back.
'
' WHAT IT SETTLES
'
' The one thing never actually measured on this link: whether the Pi's BCM 14
' electrically reaches the CR300's C2 terminal. Everything else has been checked
' and passed. The Pi emits a correct 9600 8N1 waveform, 105 us per bit against
' 104.167 nominal, idling high. The port opens, SerialOpenOK is true. The ground is
' sound, proven by 16 pulses counted from BCM 19 into P_SW. And still not one byte
' is received, with TotalBytesSeen at 0 on a raw SerialInBlock read.
'
' Note this program does NOT call SerialOpen. That is deliberate: C2 must stay a
' plain digital input for PortGet to read its level. Opening it as a serial port
' would hand the terminal to the comms driver instead.
'
' HOW TO RUN IT
'
' On the Pi:  bash /home/quaggasklip/qk_pin_toggle.sh 14 90 3
'
' That holds BCM 14 high for 3 s, then low for 3 s, for 90 seconds, so about 15
' transitions. Watch C2Changes climb in the Public table.
'
' HOW TO READ IT
'
'   C2Changes climbs to roughly 15
'       BCM 14 does reach C2. The wire is fine and the fault is entirely in the
'       serial framing, which is mine to fix.
'
'   C2Changes stays 0, and C2HighSamples or C2LowSamples is 0
'       The line is stuck at one level, so nothing is driving it. The wire does
'       not reach C2, whatever the terminal markings say. Stuck high means the
'       logger's own pull-up with an open circuit; stuck low means shorted or
'       held down.
'
'   C2Changes climbs wildly, far past 15
'       The line is floating and picking up noise, which also means it is not
'       connected to the Pi.
'
' This is the test I should have insisted on hours ago instead of reasoning from
' byte counts, which kept pointing at the wrong things.
'=============================================================================

Const SCAN_MS = 100

' PortGet stores 1 when the terminal is high and 0 when it is low.
Public C2Level As Long

' Transitions are what matter. A level read on its own can be caught mid-state
' between glances at the table, but a transition count cannot be missed.
Public C2Changes As Long

' If either of these stays 0 the line never left that state, which is the
' signature of a wire that is not connected to anything driving it.
Public C2HighSamples As Long
Public C2LowSamples As Long

' Seeded to -1 so the very first read is not counted as a transition.
Dim PrevLevel As Long

'=============================================================================
' PROGRAM
'=============================================================================

BeginProg
  PrevLevel = -1

  Scan (SCAN_MS, mSec, 0, 0)

    PortGet (C2Level, C2)

    If C2Level = 1 Then
      C2HighSamples = C2HighSamples + 1
    Else
      C2LowSamples = C2LowSamples + 1
    EndIf

    If C2Level <> PrevLevel Then
      If PrevLevel <> -1 Then C2Changes = C2Changes + 1
      PrevLevel = C2Level
    EndIf

  NextScan
EndProg
